---
import "../styles/global.css";
import { site } from "../site";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Support — OpenAdapt</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="OpenAdapt iPhone beta compatibility, pairing help, feedback, and privacy information."
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://openadapt.app/support" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="header wrap">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/">
        OpenAdapt
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href="/">
        Back to the project ↗
      </a>
    </header>
    <main class="wrap legal">
      <span class="mono">IPHONE BETA SUPPORT</span>
      <h1>A little help for your shoes.</h1>
      <p>
        OpenAdapt is an independent companion for Nike Adapt Auto Max shoes. The
        first public beta is being prepared for TestFlight review.
      </p>
      <h2>What this beta supports</h2>
      <p>
        Use an iPhone running iOS 17 or later and Nike Adapt Auto Max shoes with
        firmware 2.4.3M. This beta focuses on Bluetooth pairing and
        reconnecting, battery levels, and base light colors. Other shoe models
        and firmware are not supported.
      </p>
      <p>
        Fresh fit calibration is not available. Newly paired shoes cannot use
        app fit adjustments, saved fit modes, or fit-related Siri actions. Use
        the physical shoe buttons for fit. OpenAdapt does not update firmware or
        perform a factory reset.
      </p>
      <h2>Before pairing</h2>
      <p>
        Keep your shoes close to your iPhone and allow Bluetooth access when
        asked. Follow the app’s illuminated-button prompts, one shoe at a time.
        Pairing and interrupted recovery are experimental. Do not reset a
        working pair solely to try this beta.
      </p>
      <h2>If a connection fails</h2>
      <p>
        Check Bluetooth permission in iOS Settings and bring the shoes nearby.
        Cancel a stalled connection before trying again. If setup reports an
        interrupted pairing, stop and send feedback rather than repeatedly
        resetting or enrolling. Removing a saved pair deletes its local profile;
        it does not reset the shoes or remove their Bluetooth bond in iOS.
      </p>
      <h2>Questions and bug reports</h2>
      <p>
        OpenAdapt is open source. Browse existing questions or open an issue on{" "}
        <a href={`${site.repo}/issues`}>GitHub</a>. Issues are public, so never
        include pairing files, encryption keys, or private device identifiers.
      </p>
      <h2>Send beta feedback</h2>
      <p>
        Once you have OpenAdapt through TestFlight, open Apple’s TestFlight app,
        select OpenAdapt, then choose Send Beta Feedback to contact the
        developer. You can also send a screenshot through TestFlight’s feedback
        flow.
      </p>
      <p>
        Include your iPhone model and iOS version, shoe model and firmware, the
        steps you took, and what happened. Never send pairing files, encryption
        keys, or private device identifiers. For privacy questions, use the same
        feedback route and include “Privacy” in your message.
      </p>
      <h2>Your data stays with you</h2>
      <p>
        The app has no account, advertising, analytics, or developer-operated
        cloud service. Shoe profiles and pairing credentials remain on your
        device. Apple processes TestFlight feedback under its own terms. Read
        the <a href="/app-privacy">iPhone app privacy policy</a> and the{" "}
        <a href="/privacy">website privacy policy</a> for details.
      </p>
      <p>
        OpenAdapt is not affiliated with or endorsed by Nike. Nike and Adapt are
        trademarks of their respective owner.
      </p>
      <a class="button button-dark" href="/">
        Back to OpenAdapt →
      </a>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
